FUN_0000_ac7e (animation position-copy sub-handler, reached via ac75's byte[di+0x43] table, patch 247):
DGROUP near-offset + object base-loss (SIGSEGV).

ROOT CAUSE (asm-verified 0xac7e-0xac9d): ac7e copies a resource coord pair into the object.  si =
word[DS:0x9798] (= DAT_2000_5798, a DGROUP NEAR OFFSET that ab03 loads from the animation table); the
object is at DS:DI (di=near offset in param_1).  Ghidra typed DAT_2000_5798 as a host char* and di as a
host pointer -> wild derefs.  Fix: object = g_mem+0x1c000+di; resource = g_mem+0x1c000+DAT_2000_5798;
dword copies [si+0xc]->[di+0x49], [si+0x10]->[di+0x4d] + orw bit1 of [di+0x40].  Mission-cascade only.
